<title>UK: T&amp;N shares dip after Merrill downgrade.</title>
<headline>T&amp;N shares dip after Merrill downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK engine parts group T&amp;N Plc dropped in a rising market on Wednesday after Merrill Lynch cut its recommendation on the stock to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;accumulate,&quot; market sources said.</p>
<p>By 1230 GMT the stock was down 2-1/2p at 172-1/2.  </p>
<p>The shares bounced sharply higher at the end of November after the group announced a plan to cap its exposure to asbestos-related U.S. insurance claims. Sources said Merrill analysts argued they were now at fair value.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
